{
  "note": "The baseball seasons no game rated, 1960 to 2017, computed from the players' WAR (docs/design/baseball.md, \"Seasons before 2018: computed from WAR\"). npm run import:mlb-war (scripts/import-mlb-war.mjs) checks the pinned sources (`sources`, cached in the ignored data-src/mlb-war/) and writes one snapshot a season, scripts/data/mlb-war-seasons/<year>.json (every player with his score's inputs, his score and his birthplace), and scripts/data/mlb-war-reference.json (MLB The Show 18 to 24's overalls by role, which the scores are mapped onto, and the calibration). npm run build:mlb-seasons rates and teams each season (public/baseball/mlb-war-<year>.json); npm run build:mlb-map draws each era's map. `method` holds the rule's constants, `nations` each Lahman birth country's nation, `eras` each franchise's clubs of 1960 to 2017 (by today's franchise, scripts/data/mlb-teams.json: an era names its own id, name, code and territory (`city`) where they are not today's; `war` is the Baseball-Reference code the WAR file and Lahman use, `park` Lahman's key of the ballpark the club played most of its home games in, `base` the ballpark a tenant of another club's grows from (its point is then `home`), `lahmanName` the name Lahman gives a club whose name of the day is another), and `maps` the seasons each era map serves: a map serves consecutive seasons with the same clubs, ids, names, territories, bases and points, a ballpark renamed in place keeping its map. `seasonSource` is the source block of every season's file.",
